        "title": "Treat Philosopher's Stone as a defensive commitment",
        "situation": "When choosing an Act 1 boss relic, especially before an Act 2 boss with multiple attacking enemies.",
        "lesson": "Choose Philosopher's Stone only when the deck can reliably offset the extra enemy Strength through strong block, scaling defense, or very fast kills. Otherwise, prefer a boss relic that does not increase every enemy's damage.",
        "evidence_points": [
          "At the Act 1 boss reward, Philosopher's Stone was chosen over Pandora's Box, Calling Bell, and skipping.",
